    "narrative": "The optimization for June 25th centers on **Josh Naylor**, who sits comfortably at the top of our daily efficiency rankings with a 65.02 score. His start against Chandler is bolstered by a favorable 4.21 xERA matchup and a prime spot in the heart of the order, providing the most reliable path to RBI production. **Jose Caballero** represents our most compelling situational play; despite an 8th-order slotting penalty, his +13% platoon edge against Early and a massive +2% boost for exploiting a slow delivery\u2014crucial for our pursuit of scarce stolen bases\u2014propel his score to 59.29. Similarly, **Tyler Soderstrom** leverages his #4 spot to reach a strong 57.66 rating, proving his value as a high-floor accumulator against Roupp.\n\nThe bench remains constrained by external factors, most notably the rainout of **Corbin Carroll**, which removes our most dangerous speed threat from the board. Among available bench options, no player pushed into the top-tier efficiency threshold, as we are prioritizing game-cap preservation over marginal upgrades. We are closely monitoring the lineup for **James Wood**; while his score of 47.06 is dragged down by a tough 2.84 xERA matchup against S\u00e1nchez and poor historical BvP data, his elite xwOBA of 0.401 and the premium leadoff opportunity keep him in the mix. Owners should note that **Cole Young** and **Max Muncy** are strictly fringe starts today, both hampered by bottom-of-the-order assignments and middling efficiency scores, forcing us to lean heavily on the middle-order production of **Josh Naylor** and **Tyler Soderstrom** to carry the offensive load.",
